// #4278 B1 drill (a routine whose declaration lies about its body): the
// judged map set takes the dying receiver's credit through its hold `mh` and
// releases it inside the routine's window when the block is shared and
// copies. Re-injected, the routine no longer logs the hold move — it declares
// no consumption of the receiver while its body still releases it. The
// ownership witness is unchanged. With the routine-internal class retired,
// that release has no event to take it and nothing counts it: the RC byte
// check must refuse the frame.
effect fn main() -> Unit = {
  var m: Map[String, Int] = map.from_list([("a", 1), ("b", 2)])
  m = map.set(m, "c", 3)
  println(int.to_string(map.len(m)))
}
